.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rosregview-show 1  "rosregview-show "
.SH NAME
rosregview\-show \- Show the values of a key (default: the root). Per\-value output includes the value name, its REG_* type, and the data, decoded according to the type where possible (UTF\-16 strings, u32 little\- endian dwords, u64 little\-endian qwords, ...). Binary data is shown as a hex dump; long strings are truncated with a trailing `…`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrosregview show\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> [\fIKEY_PATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the values of a key (default: the root). Per\-value output includes the value name, its REG_* type, and the data, decoded according to the type where possible (UTF\-16 strings, u32 little\- endian dwords, u64 little\-endian qwords, ...). Binary data is shown as a hex dump; long strings are truncated with a trailing `…`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format (`human` is a typed table, `json` is machine\-readable)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to a .hiv file (Windows registry configuration unit)
.TP
[\fIKEY_PATH\fR]
Optional key path inside the hive (same convention as `list`)
